    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll start by reading the existing code to understand the structure and conventions used for the bulk-approve action, then implement the bulk-reject action following the same patterns.\nNow let me explore the internal directory structure:\nLet me examine the protocol directory to understand the HTTP adapter:\nNow let me read the existing approval.go to understand the bulk-approve implementation:\nNow let me check the app.Identity and other dependencies:\nNow I have a clear understanding of the structure. Let me implement the bulk-reject action by updating the approval.go file to add the reject handler while preserving the existing approve handler:\nNow let me verify the complete file:\nPerfect! Now let me build and test the code to ensure it compiles correctly:\nGreat! The code compiles successfully. Now let me run any tests if they exist:\nExcellent! The implementation is complete. Let me verify what I've accomplished:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added the bulk-reject action to the existing service by modifying `/Users/administrator/poc-v4-lanes/claude-haiku-4.5/kits/go-manual--009/candidate/internal/candidate/approval.go`:\n\n### Key Changes:\n\n1. **Updated the fingerprint function**: Changed from a single operation to support both operations (`bulk-approve.v3` and `bulk-reject.v4`) by accepting an operation parameter.\n\n2. **Added the reject handler**: Implemented a new `reject` closure function that mirrors the `approve` function but:\n   - Sets the target status to `'rejected'` instead of `'approved'`\n   - Returns `rejectedIds` field instead of `approvedIds`\n   - Uses the `opReject` operation identifier (`bulk-reject.v4`)\n   - Logs transitions to the `ApprovalAudit` table with `fromStatus='submitted'` and `toStatus='rejected'`\n\n3. **Registered the new route**: Added `/purchases/bulk-reject` to the `protocol.Routes` map alongside the existing `/purchases/bulk-approve`.\n\n### Implementation Details:\n\nThe reject action follows the exact same patterns as bulk-approve:\n- **Idempotency**: Uses fingerprinting and stores request hashes to detect replays\n- **Concurrency control**: Uses advisory locks to serialize concurrent requests with the same key\n- **Guarded RLS**: Only allows approvers to reject submissions from other users in the same tenant\n- **Atomic transactions**: All state changes (status update, audit record, idempotency record) happen in a single transaction\n- **Error handling**: Returns 4xx on validation failures, 409 on conflicts, and 503 on database errors\n- **UTF-8 sorting**: Returns rejectedIds sorted in UTF-8 dictionary order\n\nThe implementation preserves the existing bulk-approve API and properly enforces all the constraints specified in the schema (rejection only valid on submitted purchases, only by different users/approvers)."
